{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Oregon’s pioneering move to decriminalize personal drug use is ending as a new statute reinstates penalties for carrying small quantities of substances like fentanyl, heroin, and meth. Under HB4002, individuals caught with these drugs may face misdemeanor charges—up to half a year in jail—or be offered an alternative route involving behavioral health support and a diversion pathway to avoid fines. The law also tightens rules around selling drugs near areas like playgrounds and increases enforcement power for officers dealing with public use.\n\n***\n\nThe legislation promotes, but does not require, local jurisdictions to set up health-focused interventions to steer people away from incarceration. Supporters argue this flexibility lets regions tailor responses to their capacities, while critics warn it could lead to inconsistent outcomes across regions. Police are instructed to offer a chance at intervention only if the person has no outstanding warrants, no history of violence, and is medically stable. If those conditions are met, officers contact a specialized dispatch line to alert a mobile care team that must arrive within half an hour.\n\n***\n\nIf the care team cannot respond in time, arrest becomes the default option. Police cannot delay or linger while waiting—time is a critical factor. This tight window has raised concerns among advocates who fear that many in need may be pushed into the justice system simply due to logistical delays, not because they refuse help. The system hinges on rapid coordination, which may be difficult in rural or under-resourced areas.\n\n***\n\nIn a country where access to care varies widely, the burden often falls on those least equipped to navigate it. Some say it’s easier to go shopping for groceries than to find timely support. At what age does someone become too burdened to ask for help? When the tongue is too dry to speak, and the body too weak to walk, the system must move faster—or risk failing those it claims to serve.\n\nP.P.S The age of accountability should not depend on how far one lives from help, whether they can eat, shop, or even speak clearly—the tongue of justice must not be silenced by bureaucracy.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.00015507926582358778}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.005780527368187904}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.13278159499168396}, {"token": " move", "logprob": -0.10517826676368713}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -4.1126360883936286e-05}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -0.1169123724102974}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -0.005306445062160492}, {"token": "ize", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " personal", "logprob": -0.4623340964317322}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -9.202533692587167e-05}, {"token": " use", "logprob": -0.20157471299171448}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.00951363705098629}, {"token": " ending", "logprob": -0.3286314010620117}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.9883158206939697}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.03615459427237511}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.04044445976614952}, {"token": " statute", "logprob": -0.07059583812952042}, {"token": " reinst", "logprob": -0.9885087013244629}, {"token": "ates", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " penalties", "logprob": -0.2955035865306854}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " carrying", "logprob": -0.5310512781143188}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -0.0017791647696867585}, {"token": " quantities", "logprob": -0.0630975216627121}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " substances", "logprob": -0.06375808268785477}, {"token": " like", "logprob": -0.0001591317413840443}, {"token": " f", "logprob": -0.0027774113696068525}, {"token": "entanyl", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0005532164941541851},